Drive with the triggers, and name the pad's buttons as the pad does.

Upstream's default for a pad with shoulder buttons puts accelerate on the top face
button and brake on the left one (`src/input/gamepad_config.cpp`, the non-Switch
branch). On this pad that is Triangle and Square, which is not where a player reaches
first. Racing games on this console drive with the triggers, so under `OOPS_TARGET` a
pad that reports both triggers gets:

    R2 accelerate, L2 brake/reverse, left stick steer,
    Cross fire, Square nitro, R1 skid, Circle look back,
    Create rescue, Options pause; Cross selects and Circle goes back in menus.

A pad without triggers keeps upstream's layout. This is a default only: a profile
already saved in `input.xml` keeps its bindings until it is reset in Options.

The names STK shows for a binding - in Options, Controls and on the help page's card
(patch 0002) - are the Xbox letters upstream ships. Under `OOPS_TARGET` they are this
pad's own: Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, Create, Options, L1/R1, L2/R2, L3/R3.

